# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the output root and applies the
# headers to matching responses. Ignored by GitHub Pages, which serves no
# custom headers at all - so this covers the canonical deployment only.

# The scans in /documents/ are linked from the resume and must stay reachable:
# a reader clicking "PDF" next to an award has to get the document. They just
# should not turn up in search on their own - they carry seals, order numbers
# and personal data that belong in a resume, not in a result page.
#
# noindex rather than a robots.txt Disallow on purpose. Disallow blocks the
# crawl, and a URL that is never crawled but is linked from an indexed page
# can still be listed - as a bare URL, with no way for us to say otherwise.
# noindex is only seen if the file IS fetched, so robots.txt keeps allowing
# it. The two mechanisms cancel each other out; this is the one that removes
# a document from the index and keeps the link working.
/documents/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
